@topic savage_health_cost
@levels 15-40
@scene mid_savage_newbie
@role B class=Savage
@role C class=Healer,Shaman
@role D type=Socialite
A: new savage here, why do my buffs keep eating my health | {q} just started a savage and i keep dying before the fight even starts | savage question, are the buffs supposed to hurt this much
B: welcome. the savagery buffs cost health, that is the price | savagery buffs are paid in health. yes really
A: so i buff and then fight at three quarters health?
B: you buff, sit a moment, then pull. dont buff into a pull | buff early and sit. never buff right before the pull
C: or group with a healer who knows you are a savage | or tell your healer you buff yourself so they dont panic
?D: the healer panic is real lol
~ 25
A: which buff first? | ok which buffs matter most
B: the ones that make you swing faster and hit harder. the rest are extras when you are higher | speed of swing first, damage next. the rest when you have the points
C: and dont forget hand to hand, the buffs mean nothing with low weapon skill | keep hand to hand up with your level or you just miss a lot
?A: noted, ty
~ 30
D: how is the leveling treating you btw | where are you leveling, still around mularn?
A: west svealand now, the sveawolves are rough | west svealand, the large sveawolves hit back hard
B: savage tip, fight them one at a time and keep a buff running between pulls | pick yellows and blues one at a time, keep the buffs up
C: and sit to full health. impatience kills more savages than mobs do | rest before the pull, every single time
~ 20
A: ok got it. buff, sit, pull, dont be dumb | buff, sit, pull. got it
D: words to live by | best summary of savage play ive seen
?B: youll be fine, savages are fun once it clicks
A: ty all, going back out | thanks, heading back to the wolves
C: send a tell if you need a heal, im in myrkwood | im nearby if you die, rez on request
B: gl out there!

